      "description": "Watch Napoli vs Bologna highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 14, 2026. High Tension at the Start On September 14, 2026 , SSC Napoli and Bologna faced off in a Serie A encounter that showcased tactical discipline and high-stakes drama. Both teams entered the pitch with clear structures, looking to establish dominance in the midfield from the opening whistle. The match saw its first major turning point early on. In the 8th minute, Bologna thought they had taken the lead through Arthur Theate , but the goal was chalked off following a VAR review for offside. This let-off galvanized Napoli , who began to control more of the ball, though clear-cut chances remained rare in a physical first half that saw Mikel Amondarain receive a yellow card for a robust challenge. Lobotka Breaks the Deadlock The second half saw Napoli turn up the pressure, aided by the tactical introduction of Noa Lang and Costantino Favasuli . The home side’s creative engine, Kevin De Bruyne , began to dictate play, consistently delivering dangerous balls from corners and open play that tested the Bologna backline. The breakthrough finally arrived in the 66th minute. A brilliant sequence of play saw Kevin De Bruyne provide a key pass to Costantino Favasuli , who squared the ball for Stanislav Lobotka . The midfielder made no mistake, finishing clinicaly with his right foot to put Napoli ahead. The goal reflected Napoli's growing dominance, as they maintained nearly 59% possession throughout much of the half. Defensive Solidity and Final Whistle As the clock ticked down, Bologna pushed for an equalizer, making several substitutions including the introduction of Jens Odgaard . However, the Napoli defense, anchored by Amir Rrahmani and Rafa Marin , stood firm. Marin was particularly impressive in the dying moments, intercepting crucial crosses aimed into the penalty area. Despite five minutes of added time and late pressure from the visitors, Napoli managed the game professionally. Mathias Olivera replaced De Bruyne in the 88th minute to bolster the defense, ensuring that the hosts kept a clean sheet and secured all three points in a hard-fought contest."
